---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Workflows"
   summary="Copy the commands for a criterion check, page scan, screen reader session, or MCP integration. Each workflow states what its result can prove."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="split panel" id="drive-a-session">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Workflow 1</p>
            <h2>Drive a screen reader</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            Use the driver when you need to navigate elements, send keystrokes, or read spoken
            output directly.
         </p>
         <pre><code>a1 sr start --json
a1 sr focus --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --app "Google Chrome" --json
a1 sr next --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --json
a1 sr read --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --json
a1 sr stop --session &lt;sessionId&gt; --json</code></pre>
         <p>
            Open the page before starting a real VoiceOver or NVDA session. For a simulated run,
            start the virtual target with <code>--allow-virtual</code> and <code>--url</code>.
         </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Keep the output</div>
         <p class="aside-note">Save the spoken phrase log with the route, actions, browser, and screen reader used in the test.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel" id="agent-and-mcp">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Workflow 2</p>
            <h2>Run the tools from an agent</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            Connect the MCP server when an AI agent or editor should call the screen reader, axe,
            WCAG, and inspect tools directly.
         </p>
         <pre><code>npx -y a11ied mcp</code></pre>
         <p>Follow the <a href="/agent-workflows">AI agent guide</a> for client configuration and practical prompts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Local process</div>
         <p class="aside-note">The server communicates over stdio. It does not listen on a network port.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel" id="gather-evidence">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Workflow 3</p>
            <h2>Scan a page with axe</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            Run axe against a development URL for fast, repeatable checks. Keep the JSON output with
            the pull request or test report.
         </p>
         <pre><code>a1 axe --url http://localhost:3000 --level AA --json</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Choose a scope</div>
         <p class="aside-note">Use exactly one of <code>--level</code>, <code>--criterion</code>, or one or more <code>--rule</code> flags.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel" id="check-one-criterion">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Workflow 4</p>
            <h2>Check one WCAG criterion</h2>
         </div>
         <p>
            Look up the criterion, check its coverage, inspect the page, then run any mapped axe rules.
         </p>
         <pre><code>a1 wcag show 1.1.1 --json
a1 wcag coverage 1.1.1 --json
a1 inspect criterion 1.1.1 --url http://localhost:3000 --json
a1 axe --criterion 1.1.1 --url http://localhost:3000 --json</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Read coverage first</div>
         <p class="aside-note">If coverage is <code>hybrid</code> or <code>manual</code>, follow the returned strategy instead of treating axe as the whole test.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Before a real driver session</p>
         <h2>Open the page in the target browser</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         VoiceOver and NVDA operate the browser window already on screen. Navigate to the route,
         wait for the interface to finish loading, then start the session and focus that browser.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
